	(text "F31 CLOSES HERE, AND IT CLOSES ON THE DATASHEET'S OWN WORDS -- no battery, no charger.\nPin 23 BAT_IN: 'Power supply input; voltage range: 3.2V to 4.2V. Source can either be a\nLi-ion battery OR ANY OTHER POWER RAIL ON THE HOST BOARD.' A direct rail feed is\nBLESSED, not merely tolerated, so the charger path is not needed and ADAP_IN stays\nfloating per its own pin description.\n\nTHE ARITHMETIC, END TO END:\n  +3V6_BT actual = 3.584 V (AP2127K-ADJ, VREF 0.8 V +/-2 %, 34.8k/10k -- V-23).\n  Worst case across VREF tol + both divider legs: ~3.44 V to ~3.73 V.\n  BAT_IN window: 3.2 V to 4.2 V.  ->  clears the floor by 240 mV and the ceiling by 470 mV.\n  Current, Table 9-12: A2DP 12.05 mA typ; SCO 14.1 mA; CONTINUOUS TX 59 mA WORST.\n  AP2127 is a 300 mA part -> 5x margin on the worst RF case, and the LDO dissipates\n  (5.0 - 3.584) x 0.059 = 84 mW, trivial in SOT-23-5.\nTHE OLD 100 mA ESTIMATE IN S7.1 WAS CONSERVATIVE BY ~1.7x. It is not corrected here --\nthe rail was sized on it and the margin is free -- but the measured number is now on\nrecord so a future cost pass does not 'discover' the headroom and delete it.\n\nSYS_PWR (24) and VDD_IO (25) are 'for internal use only, do not connect'. They are\nexplicit no-connects, NOT tied to anything convenient -- the temptation is to bridge\nSYS_PWR to the rail because the name reads like an output that wants a cap."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 430.53000000000003 59.69 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "76af543b-0fa1-5bbf-9601-33912a2ce5af")
	)
	(text "FLASHING IS COPPER, NOT INTENTION (F32). The module ships in EMBEDDED mode; this design\nis HOST mode. Nothing on this sheet works until the config is flashed, so the path to\nflash it is drawn rather than assumed:\n  * UART_RXD (29) / UART_TXD (30) reach the ESP32 AND a test header, so the Config Tool\n    can drive the module directly with the ESP32 held in reset.\n  * PIN 31 (P3_4/UART_RTS) IS ALSO THE APPLICATION / TEST MODE STRAP. Stuffing pair:\n        POPULATED 10k to GND      = Application mode (normal operation)\n        DNP 10k to +3V6_BT        = Test mode (programming)\n    Two positions, one populated, so mode entry is a soldering iron and not a cut trace.\n  * BM83_RST_N is brought out with a series 1k, so the tool can toggle reset.\n  * PROCEDURE, INCLUDING WHO FLASHES AND WHEN, IS A BRINGUP.md LINE -- copper only makes\n    it possible. F32 asked for the production-step decision and that is still open:\n    factory-programmed part, or a board-level step. THIS SHEET DOES NOT DECIDE IT.\n\nCONFIG-DEPENDENT PINS CARRY '*' IN THE SYMBOL (F32 convention). This is the ONE part on\nthe board whose PINOUT is firmware-dependent, so F28's 'every pin dispositioned' needs a\nsecond dimension here: a pin can be correctly dispositioned FOR THE WRONG CONFIG. Every\n'*' pin above is a no-connect, which is the only disposition that stays valid in both\nmodes -- deliberately, not by accident."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 430.53000000000003 190.5 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "4556d7c7-5453-51af-892b-26869a2c1f41")
	)
	(text "I2S: THE MODULE IS A SLAVE, AND THE DECREE SAYS SO TWICE.\nS4 [HARD] map: SDATA_IN1 = BM83, I2S stereo, 2 channels -> ASRC.\nS3: '... BM83 I2S port (BM83 configured as I2S slave).'\nSo SCLK1 (3) and RFS1 (2) are INPUTS here, driven by the DSP's SDATA_IN1 port clocks, and\nDT1 (4) carries A2DP audio toward the DSP. T1-56 confirms this is possible: SCLK1 and RFS1\nare I/O, so the module can be either -- it is CONFIGURATION that makes it a slave, which\nmeans this is another line the flashed config must get right (F32 again).\nMCLK1 (5) is OUTPUT-ONLY per T1-56 and we are the clock master, so it is unused.\n\n*** THE RECOVERED BLUETOOTH CLOCK NEVER ENTERS THE AUDIO CLOCK TREE. *** The module's\nstream is asynchronous to our 48 kHz by nature, and S3 [HARD] routes it through the\nADAU1466's on-chip ASRC -- 'no exceptions'. Slaving the module to our clocks does NOT\nmake the STREAM synchronous; it only makes the WIRE synchronous. The ASRC is what absorbs\nthe rate difference, and removing it because 'the port is slaved now' would be the exact\nmistake F1 caught on the S/PDIF path.\nDR1 (1) is an unused INPUT and is tied to GND rather than left floating (F21)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 430.53000000000003 330.2 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "d6651278-c453-57cc-a6cc-d56844ac214e")
	)
	(text "LAYOUT INPUTS -- recorded now because they constrain PLACEMENT before any footprint\nexists, and placement is decided long before the footprint pass.\n  * ANTENNA KEEPOUT [HARD]: no copper, no components, no ground plane under the module's\n    PCB antenna. Exact dimensions are V-12, whose pages are rendered but NOT YET READ --\n    they belong with the footprint, not here.\n  * TWO 2.4 GHz ANTENNAS ON ONE BOARD. S8 [HARD]: separate them as far as geometry\n    allows, DO NOT STACK. This module and the ESP32-S3-WROOM-1 are both radios with\n    integrated antennas and they share a band. The constraint is on the BOARD OUTLINE,\n    which is still Block D UNSET -- so this note exists to make sure the outline, when it\n    arrives, is chosen with two antenna corners in mind rather than discovered to lack\n    them.\n  * The module edge should face a board edge. That is a placement consequence of the\n    keepout, not an extra rule."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 430.53000000000003 459.74 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "57d1b67b-5ae4-5a48-80cc-c0d40c7d0241")
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
